  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian House of Representatives (DPR RI) has officially enacted the Law on Asset Seizure Related to Corruption and Other Crimes. This legislation, which reached final approval after an 18-year deliberative period, is described as a major development in the state's efforts to recover financial losses stemming from criminal activities. While supporters view the move as a significant step toward more progressive anti-corruption enforcement, it has faced scrutiny regarding its implementation. Specifically, reports indicate that the law contains provisions, such as those in Article 72, which limit its application to older corruption cases. Concurrently, the Indonesian Corruption Watch (ICW) has submitted formal complaints to the House's Ethics Council (MKD) against Puan Maharani and Habiburokhman, alleging ethical breaches during the deliberation of the draft bill. The Corruption Eradication Commission (KPK) has publicly declared its commitment to enforcing the new statute.",
